---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Main from "@/components/Main.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n";
import config from "@/config";

const locale = Astro.currentLocale ?? config.site.lang;
---

<Layout
  title={`Editorial Process | ${config.site.title}`}
  description="How The Noise Filter verifies facts, filters viral noise, and enforces rigorous editorial standards."
>
  <Header />
  <Main pageTitle="Editorial Process" eyebrow="Trust" class="app-prose">
    <p>
      The Noise Filter is an independent publication designed to turn down the
      internet's volume knob. We provide calm, verified explainers on complex
      technology shifts, platform rollouts, consumer subscription traps, and
      digital policy for regular adults who want the signal without the noise.
    </p>

    <h2>The Signal Framework: What Changed, Matters, and to Ignore</h2>
    <p>
      Every explainer on The Noise Filter begins with a structured 3-part Quick
      Filter:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What Changed:</strong> The verifiable event, firmware rollout,
        pricing change, or regulatory filing that actually occurred.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Why It Matters:</strong> The practical, financial, or security
        consequence for everyday consumers and professionals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What to Ignore:</strong> The viral exaggeration, speculative
        panic, or corporate marketing spin that can be safely disregarded.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Within every deep dive, we rigorously separate four categories of information:
      <em>Confirmed Facts</em>, <em>Active Rollout Realities</em>, <em>Unclear or
      Pending Questions</em>, and <em>Industry Speculation</em>.
    </p>

    <h2>Primary Source Hierarchy</h2>
    <p>
      We do not aggregate third-party rumors or rephrase unverified blog posts.
      Our research follows a strict evidence hierarchy:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Official Technical & Support Documentation:</strong> Manufacturer
        spec sheets, developer documentation, API changelogs, and official support
        articles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Regulatory & Legal Filings:</strong> Formal dockets and orders
        from government bodies (e.g., FERC, FTC, SEC, FCC, South Korea's KCC and
        National Geographic Information Institute).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Standards & Industry Specifications:</strong> Engineering standards
        (IEEE, FIDO Alliance, JEDEC), public utility tariffs, and peer-reviewed
        research.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reputable Secondary Reporting:</strong> Used strictly for context
        and chronological tracking, never as the sole basis for technical or
        financial assertions.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Visual Authenticity & Anti-PPT Rule</h2>
    <p>
      We reject generic AI stock illustrations (such as repetitive laptops on
      sterile desks) and generic corporate slide templates. Our explanatory
      visuals are selected to match the physical reality of the subject:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Physical Reality & Reference Photography:</strong> Authentic
        hardware, component cross-sections, and facility photography verified
        under commercial public domain, CC0, or CC-BY licensing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Real Software & Interface Captures:</strong> Exact mobile settings
        menus, platform toggles, and official repository assets.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Minimalist Decision Schematics:</strong> High-contrast, clean
        flowcharts and mathematical comparisons that make costs, trade-offs, and
        decision trees immediately transparent.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI Assistance with Mandatory Human Gate</h2>
    <p>
      We believe in ethical, transparent use of technology. Artificial intelligence
      tools are utilized to assist with information synthesis, outline organization,
      and readability analysis.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, <strong>no article is published autonomously</strong>. Under our
      standard operating policy, every piece passes through a mandatory human editorial
      gate. The human editor:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Verifies all numerical claims, pricing details, and regulatory citations against primary sources.</li>
      <li>Removes speculative certainty and ensures nuanced boundary conditions are clearly stated.</li>
      <li>Eliminates promotional fluff and enforces an analytical, calm tone.</li>
      <li>Confirms that no fabricated first-hand experience, synthetic benchmark data, or fictitious interviews are present.</li>
      <li>Makes the final, binding publication decision.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For historical articles created during earlier prototyping stages without
      pre-publish review packets, retrospective editorial audits are conducted
      against these exact standards to verify factual integrity and ensure source accuracy.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and Dynamic Updates</h2>
    <p>
      Technology platforms and subscription terms evolve constantly. Each article
      carries an explicit verification date note. When material policies change,
      we update the analysis and record the modification.
    </p>
    <p>
      Readers who spot factual discrepancies or broken references are encouraged
      to submit a report via our public tracker:
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/natekeem/the-noise-filter/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Submit a correction via GitHub Issues
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Commercial Independence</h2>
    <p>
      The Noise Filter does not accept sponsored content, paid guest posts,
      affiliate marketing links, or compensation for favorable coverage. Our
      editorial evaluations are made solely on technical merits, regulatory
      realities, and consumer interests.
    </p>
    <p>
      For questions about site policies, see our{" "}
      <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, "disclosure")}>Editorial Disclosure</a>{" "}
      and <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, "privacy")}>Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </Main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
